      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=civileats.com&amp;sz=128\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<div class=\"rss-custom-item\" style=\"font-family:sans-serif;line-height:1.3;\"><img alt=\"The Conservation Fund has permanently protected Z-Farm on Chicago’s South Side, a working farm that has spent the last two years bringing local food back to the community. The land now belongs to Urban Growers Collective, the nonprofit that has farmed it since 2024, giving the organization permanent ownership and ensuring the property will stay farmland for good.\" src=\"https://civileats.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/261013-South-Chicago-Farmland-Permanently-Protected-hero-700x466.jpg\" style=\"height:auto;margin-bottom:12px;display:block;\"/><span style=\"font-style:italic;color:#555555;font-size:14px;display:block;margin-bottom:4px;\">By Kelly Larsen • October 13, 2026</span><span style=\"font-size:16px;color:#222222;display:block;margin-bottom:8px;\">Conservation efforts can help prevent the loss of land that is currently stymying small farming.</span><span style=\"display:block;\"><a href=\"https://civileats.com/2026/10/13/op-ed-theres-a-future-for-farming-in-chicago-and-cities-beyond/\" style=\"font-weight:bold;text-decoration:underline;color:#111111;\">Read the full article →</a></span></div>",
